some(), an array method
-some method is an array object property use test each element on its array array if its satisfies a specific condition.
some() has two parameter, first is the callback function, the callback function is the assigned to check each element satisfies the condition,
it only return a boolean (true or false). and the callback function also have a 3 parameter (element,index,array).
The second parameter of this method is thisArgs, this parameter is optional, most dev dont use it, but this parameter represent the value as this keyword
inside the block statement. So to summarize this function usage, it is used for checking or condition to check the array depending 
on the condition, given to the callback function.